# <client project root>/.env — PER-CLIENT configuration
#
# Which Search Console property to report on, and how. NO CREDENTIALS EVER LIVE
# HERE: the OAuth client, refresh token and service-account key are shared and
# belong in ~/clients/agency.env.
#
#   cp client.env.example ~/clients/<client>/.env
#
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. Replace the property with the client's own.

# --- REQUIRED: the Search Console property, EXACTLY as Search Console shows it.
#
# Two kinds, and they are different properties with different data:
#
#   Domain property     — every subdomain, both protocols, one dataset
#       GSC_SITE_URL=sc-domain:example.com
#
#   URL-prefix property — exactly that scheme, host and path prefix
#       GSC_SITE_URL=https://www.example.com/
#
# https://example.com/ and https://www.example.com/ are NOT the same property.
# The trailing slash is required. A bare hostname is rejected rather than
# guessed. Copy the value from the property switcher in Search Console.
#
# To see what the agency identity can actually read:
#   python3 scripts/check_config.py --list-sites
GSC_SITE_URL=https://www.example.com/

# --- OPTIONAL: display name for the report header.
# CLIENT_NAME=Example Company

# --- OPTIONAL: brand terms, comma separated. WITHOUT THIS THERE IS NO
# BRANDED/NON-BRANDED ANALYSIS — the skill will not guess which queries are
# branded, because every figure derived from a guess inherits it.
#
# Include every variation worth matching: the brand, abbreviations, the domain,
# common misspellings, and any sub-brand or product name that functions as one.
# Matching is case-insensitive substring matching.
# GSC_BRAND_TERMS=example company,examplecompany,example co,exampl company,example.com

# --- OPTIONAL: the client's primary market, ISO-3166-1 alpha-3 as Search Console
# reports it (usa, gbr, can, aus, deu...). Used to judge whether geographic
# movement is worth a section.
# GSC_PRIMARY_COUNTRY=usa

# --- OPTIONAL: the Search Console surface for the main report. Default: web.
# Changing this changes what the KPI table describes; it does not add a surface.
# GSC_SEARCH_TYPE=web

# --- OPTIONAL: additional surfaces to retrieve and report SEPARATELY. They are
# never added into the web totals. Discover and googleNews have no query
# dimension and no meaningful average position.
# GSC_EXTRA_SEARCH_TYPES=image,discover

# --- OPTIONAL: period length in days for both windows. Default 30.
# GSC_REPORT_DAYS=30

# --- OPTIONAL: hold both windows back by this many days. Worth setting on
# properties where the freshest finalised days still visibly move. Both windows
# shift together, so they stay comparable.
# GSC_LAG_DAYS=0

# --- OPTIONAL: rows per API request. Maximum and default 25000. Lower it only to
# be gentle on a shared quota.
# GSC_ROW_LIMIT=25000

# --- OPTIONAL: run URL Inspection on the worst-declining pages. Off by default:
# it is a point-in-time index check with a real daily quota, not a crawler.
# GSC_INSPECT_URLS=false
# GSC_MAX_URL_INSPECTIONS=10

# --- Other reports-* skills may add their own keys to this same file (a Google
# Ads customer ID, a GA4 property ID). Keep credentials out of all of them.
